(B[m[38;2;224;226;234m[48;2;20;22;27m- (B[m[38;2;224;226;234m[48;2;20;22;27m{motion}(B[m[38;2;224;226;234m[48;2;20;22;27m      A command that moves the cursor.  These are explained in
                (B[0;4m[38;2;224;226;234m[48;2;20;22;27m]8;id=3790209026;https://neovim.io/doc/user/helptag/?tag=motion.txt\motion.txt(B[m[38;2;224;226;234m[48;2;20;22;27m]8;;\.   
                - Examples:[18X
                  - (B[m[38;2;140;248;247m[48;2;20;22;27mw(B[m[38;2;224;226;234m[48;2;20;22;27m           to start of next word
                  - (B[m[38;2;140;248;247m[48;2;20;22;27mb(B[m[38;2;224;226;234m[48;2;20;22;27m           to begin of current word
                  - (B[m[38;2;140;248;247m[48;2;20;22;27m4j(B[m[38;2;224;226;234m[48;2;20;22;27m          four lines down
                  - (B[m[38;2;140;248;247m[48;2;20;22;27m/The<CR>(B[m[38;2;224;226;234m[48;2;20;22;27m    to next occurrence of "The"
                - This is used after an (B[0;4m[38;2;224;226;234m[48;2;20;22;27m]8;id=3790209027;https://neovim.io/doc/user/helptag/?tag=operator\operator(B[m[38;2;224;226;234m[48;2;20;22;27m]8;;\ command to move over the
                  text that is to be operated upon.[K
                  - If the motion includes a count and the operator also has[K
                    a count, the two counts are multiplied.  For example:[K
                    "2d3w" deletes six words.[K
                  - The motion can be backwards, e.g. "db" to delete to the[K
                    start of the word.[K
                  - The motion can also be a mouse click.  The mouse is not[K
                    supported in every terminal though.[K
                  - The ":omap" command can be used to map characters while an[K
                    operator is pending.[K
                  - Ex commands can be used to move the cursor.  This can be[K
