(B[m[38;2;196;198;205m[48;2;44;46;51mfixture.lua [+]                                               9,3            Bot[2 q[?1002h[?1006h[1;49H[?25h[?25l[24;70H(B[m[38;2;224;226;234m[48;2;20;22;27m^F[1;49H[?25h[?25l[24;70H  [1;20r[H[18M[r[3;1H                    used to call a function that does some complicated motion.[K
                    The motion is always charwise exclusive, no matter what[K
                    ":" command is used.  This means it's impossible to[K
                    include the last character of a line without the line[K
                    break (unless (B[m[38;2;224;226;234m[48;2;20;22;27m]8;id=3790209028;https://neovim.io/doc/user/helptag/?tag='virtualedit'\'(B[0;4m[38;2;224;226;234m[48;2;20;22;27mvirtualedit(B[m[38;2;224;226;234m[48;2;20;22;27m'(B[m[38;2;224;226;234m[48;2;20;22;27m]8;;\ is set). If the Ex command[K
                    changes the text before where the operator starts or jumps[K
                    to another buffer the result is unpredictable.  It is[K
                    possible to change the text further down.  Jumping to[K
                    another buffer is possible if the current buffer is not[K
                    unloaded.[K
